  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "IMCSC takes one scaled reciprocal of IMSIN(z) rather than IMDIV(\"1\", IMSIN(z)), returning #NUM! at 0 and |re| >= 2^27",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, IMCSC(inumber) computes z_sin = sin(inumber) (rejecting |re| >= 2^27 with #NUM!), returns #NUM! when z_sin = 0+0i (such as 0), and forms 1 / z_sin via a single scaled reciprocal 1 / (a + b * ratio) multiplied by ratio (which differs after rounding from IMDIV's two separate quotients), flushing subnormal components to 0. All 1,209 full-bank IMCSC rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/w111-extended-regenerated-20260929/answers-imcsc.json.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20430) and Excel 16.0.20527.20088 (prefix_metadata row 118); 1,209/1,209 full-bank rows match.",
